{
  "//": "Seccomp allowlist for the pvpgn container: bnetd and the entrypoint that renders its config. defaultAction denies with EPERM. bnetd is a single-process network daemon: it needs sockets, epoll/poll/select, file I/O for the account store and config, memory, signals, and its interval timer (setitimer drives every in-game timer: keepalives, latency checks, delayed disconnects). The entrypoint adds the shell's fork/exec/pipe. Denied by omission: the process-escape calls (ptrace, mount, unshare, setns, bpf, keyctl, kexec, module loading) and changing user or group id, which a non-root container never does. Checked by booting the daemon under this profile on a read-only root and comparing its log with an unconfined run; widen it only when a legitimate call is denied.",
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
  "archMap": [
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
      "subArchitectures": [
        "SCMP_ARCH_X86",
        "SCMP_ARCH_X32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_AARCH64",
      "subArchitectures": [
        "SCMP_ARCH_ARM"
      ]
    }
  ],
